  "id": "COMPOUND:485 - PROTEIN:813",
  "verbalization": "Oxycodone is implicated in the relationship with the Kappa-type opioid receptor through a multi-step mechanism involving the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C. This receptor is a target of Oxycodone, as well as of 3-Methylfentanyl and Ginkgolide A, all of which are linked to the Kappa-type opioid receptor. The presence of multiple targets that ultimately converge on the Kappa-type opioid receptor suggests a potential role for Oxycodone in modulating this receptor, possibly through a shared signaling pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, biologically plausible link, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The involvement of different compounds targeting the same receptor highlights the complexity of opioid receptor regulation and the potential for Oxycodone to exert its effects through a variety of pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Oxycodone may influence the Kappa-type opioid receptor, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action.",
